### Auth endpoints — tested THROUGH the API Gateway (Ocelot).
### The browser/clients only ever call the gateway at :7000.
### (You can also hit the Auth service directly at http://localhost:7001 for Swagger.)

@gateway = http://localhost:7000

### 1. Register a new user
# Returns 200 with a JWT token on success, or 409 if username/email exists.
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "student",
  "email": "student@lab.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### 2. Login
# @name login   <-- names this response so we can reuse its token below.
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "student",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### 3. The token is now available as:
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 4. (Negative test) Login with a wrong password -> 401 Unauthorized
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "student",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 5. Gateway health check
GET {{gateway}}/health
